{"3287230": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Helen Keller Simulator", "steam_appid": 3287230, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Helen Keller Simulator</strong> is an experimental exploration game where you navigate a world without sight or sound.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With no visuals and no audio cues, you must rely entirely on whatever you stumble upon.<br>Let subtle tooltips guide you as you collect items, avoid unseen dangers, and traverse unfamiliar environments with no clear map or direction.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each new area is only revealed as you find it, challenging your sense of space, memory, and orientation. Death is possible, and progress depends on learning how to feel your way through the darkness.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a game about winning or a linear story.  It’s an abstract, difficult experience meant to immerse you in an unfamiliar way of perceiving a world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This is a <strong>parody game</strong> and a work of fiction. It contains <strong>no visuals, no sound, and no characters</strong>—so any resemblance to real people is purely in your imagination. The game is <strong>not endorsed by Helen Keller, her estate, or anyone else (seen or unseen)</strong>. All references are <strong>deliberately exaggerated for comedic effect</strong>.  If you take a look, <strong>I’m sure it won’t be clear to see</strong>...</h2>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Helen Keller Simulator</strong> is an experimental exploration game where you navigate a world without sight or sound.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With no visuals and no audio cues, you must rely entirely on whatever you stumble upon.<br>Let subtle tooltips guide you as you collect items, avoid unseen dangers, and traverse unfamiliar environments with no clear map or direction.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each new area is only revealed as you find it, challenging your sense of space, memory, and orientation. Death is possible, and progress depends on learning how to feel your way through the darkness.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is not a game about winning or a linear story.  It’s an abstract, difficult experience meant to immerse you in an unfamiliar way of perceiving a world.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This is a <strong>parody game</strong> and a work of fiction. It contains <strong>no visuals, no sound, and no characters</strong>—so any resemblance to real people is purely in your imagination. The game is <strong>not endorsed by Helen Keller, her estate, or anyone else (seen or unseen)</strong>. All references are <strong>deliberately exaggerated for comedic effect</strong>.  If you take a look, <strong>I’m sure it won’t be clear to see</strong>...</h2>", "short_description": "Explore a world without your eyes and ears to guide you. Uncover the secrets this world has to offer, hoard all the items you can find or get lost trying.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3287230/header.jpg?t=1785531161", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3287230/64da3bdb801665405f68a4aa102ae91c16936247/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1785531161", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3287230/64da3bdb801665405f68a4aa102ae91c16936247/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1785531161", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 7<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> x86_32 CPU with SSE2 instructions, x86_64 CPU, ARMv8 CPU<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 1 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Integrated graphics with full Vulkan 1.0 su